bug_descriptions |bug_id, line_num, content|
    web_render_lcd_run_end_ink_column_not_painted_2026-11-28, 0, "Chrome 159 at 1x paints the last ink column of the last glyph of an LCD text run; the engine leaves it white. Fixture (absolutely positioned p at left:10px, Liberation Sans, color #000 on white): 16 px 'a b g m o p s y' loses (115,12) cff7ff, 16 px 'employs gamma' loses (127,44) 4f9fdf, 13 px 'a b g m o p s y  employs gamma' loses (198,67) e7ffff, the same at 14 px loses (212,92) 67bfef. A lone 'a' loses (19,134) c7efff and ' a' loses (23,164) 4f9fdf."
    web_render_lcd_run_end_ink_column_not_painted_2026-11-28, 1, "Facts: the column is painted when more text follows in the same run ('employs gamma l': 0 mismatching px on the a), and an explicit width:300px on the block does not bring it back, so it is the run's own extent and not the box. Present on the base (85ea9caddc5) and unchanged by the autohinter port; after the port it is the whole residual of the fixture (1 px per row). The run START has the same gap: A as the first glyph of a line at left:10px loses its left fringe column, (9,54) fff7cf at 16 px and (9,143) fff7cf at 13 px (glyph fixture a..z / A..Z / 0..9 at 13, 14, 16 px and Bold: 8 mismatching px in all after the port, every one a first or last ink column of a run)."
    web_render_lcd_run_end_ink_column_not_painted_2026-11-28, 2, "Not established: whether the run bitmap is sized from the phase-0 cell widths (font_renderer.spl, max_x = gx + glyph.width) while the phased LCD cell of the last glyph is one column wider, or the draw rect is cut at the run advance. Check both before fixing."

